RetexTest.WcChildren: grid

*grid.wcClass: Gridbox
*grid.WcChildren: label quit
*weightx: 1
*weighty: 1


*label.gridx: 0
*label.gridy: 0
*label.wcClass: Wlabel 
*label.label: test ${ \\left( \\frac{2^x}{x} \\right) }$ \n\n \\hbox{ \\vcenter{\\parbox{300pt}{This text should be next to the icon. It spans several lines and is wrapped correctly inside a parbox. This demonstrates the power of nested boxes in our TeX engine.}} \\vcenter{\\includesvg{../LuaRunner/alert.svg}{100pt}{100pt}} } \n\n{\\Huge It} now supports multiple paragraphs! This is achieved by detecting double newlines in the input text and processing each paragraph separately. \n\n \\hfill \\vcenter{\\includesvg{../LuaRunner/alert.svg}{100pt}{100pt}} \\hfill \n\nEach paragraph is automatically wrapped to the width of the widget, ensuring that the text remains readable regardless of the window size. This demonstrates a key feature of the TeX-inspired layout engine.\n\nThe engine uses boxes, glue, and penalties to achieve high-quality typesetting, even in this lightweight implementation.
*label.alignment: 3
*label.fontFace: Serif
*label.fontSize: 16
*label.width: 500
*label.height: 400

*quit.gridx: 0
*quit.gridy: 1
*quit.wcClass: Wbutton
*quit.label: Quit
*quit.callback: WcQuit
*quit.fontFace: Serif
*quit.fontSize: 10

